      en: { title: 'Santo Domingo Malecón: waterfront walking guide', subtitle: 'The Caribbean seafront along Avenida George Washington', intro: 'The Malecón is a long urban coastline with Caribbean views, monuments and distinct stretches for walking.', history: 'Avenida George Washington became a major modern link between Santo Domingo and the Caribbean coast, gathering landmarks along the seafront.', visit: 'Notice the horizon, sea walls and monuments within your chosen segment rather than treating the entire road as one stop.', transport: 'Navigate to a specific point on Avenida George Washington; the waterfront is long and traffic varies.', tips: 'Expect sun, wind and sea spray. Use designated crossings and stay away from moving traffic.', manager: 'The public waterfront road and promenade involve municipal responsibilities and competent road and coastal infrastructure authorities.', architecture: 'The defining experience is the relationship between boulevard, sea wall, monuments and the Caribbean horizon.', route: 'Start at an accessible public seafront point, follow a continuous sidewalk segment and return using marked crossings.', photoTips: 'Frame the coastline with a recognizable monument or boulevard feature, ideally in late-afternoon light.', faq: ['Is it one lookout? No, it is a long coastal corridor.', 'Can it be walked? Yes, use established sidewalks.', 'Where should I start? Choose one mapped segment.'] },
